<Layout
title="Privacy Policy | CreateLoom"
description="Learn how CreateLoom handles information, browser storage, contact requests, analytics and advertising."

>

  <article class="legal container">

```
<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p class="updated">
  Last updated: September 12, 2026
</p>

<p>
  CreateLoom ("CreateLoom", "we", "us", or "our") operates
  <strong>createloom.vercel.app</strong> and provides AI image
  prompts, creator resources, guides and related content.
</p>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy explains what information may be processed when
  you visit or interact with CreateLoom and how that information may
  be used. By using the website, you acknowledge the practices
  described in this policy.
</p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom is primarily a static content website. We do not require
  visitors to create an account in order to browse prompts, read
  articles or use the website's core features.
</p>

<p>
  Depending on the features and services enabled on the website,
  information may be processed when you voluntarily provide it, such
  as when you contact us or otherwise communicate with us.
</p>

<p>
  We do not intentionally request sensitive personal information
  through the website.
</p>

<h2>2. Browser storage and preferences</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom may use browser storage, including local storage, to
  remember certain preferences and features on your device.
</p>

<p>
  For example, the website may store locally saved or favorited
  prompts so that they can remain available during future visits from
  the same browser.
</p>

<p>
  This locally stored information is stored by your browser and is
  not, by itself, transmitted to CreateLoom's servers.
</p>

<h2>3. Cookies</h2>

<p>
  The current core CreateLoom experience does not require cookies for
  visitors to browse the prompt library or read our content.
</p>

<p>
  If cookies or similar technologies are introduced through analytics,
  advertising, embedded services, affiliate programs or other
  third-party services, this Privacy Policy will be updated to
  describe their use and purpose.
</p>

<h2>4. Advertising</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom may use third-party advertising services in the future,
  including Google AdSense. If advertising is enabled, advertising
  providers and their partners may use cookies or similar technologies
  to serve and measure advertisements.
</p>

<p>
  Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads
  based on a user's previous visits to this website or other websites.
  Google's advertising cookies may enable Google and its partners to
  serve advertisements based on users' visits to this and other
  websites.
</p>

<p>
  If personalized advertising is enabled, users may opt out of
  personalized advertising through Google's Ads Settings or through
  other applicable opt-out mechanisms provided by advertising
  providers.
</p>

<p>
  When advertising is actually enabled on CreateLoom, this policy will
  be updated with the applicable advertising providers and any
  additional disclosures required by those services.
</p>

<h2>5. Analytics</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom may use analytics services in the future to understand
  website traffic, page performance and how visitors use the site.
</p>

<p>
  If an analytics service is enabled, the relevant service may collect
  information such as pages visited, approximate location, device or
  browser information, referral information and interaction data,
  depending on the provider's configuration and applicable privacy
  settings.
</p>

<p>
  This policy will be updated to identify the specific analytics
  providers used on the website when such services are enabled.
</p>

<h2>6. Third-party services and links</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom may link to or use third-party websites, services,
  platforms or tools. These third parties operate under their own
  privacy policies and terms.
</p>

<p>
  CreateLoom is not responsible for the privacy practices, security or
  content of third-party websites. Visitors should review the privacy
  policies of third-party services before providing them with personal
  information.
</p>

<h2>7. Data security</h2>

<p>
  We take reasonable measures appropriate to the nature of the website
  to protect information that is voluntarily provided to us.
  However, no method of transmission or electronic storage can be
  guaranteed to be completely secure.
</p>

<h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>

<p>
  CreateLoom is not directed toward children under the age required by
  applicable law to provide consent for online services. We do not
  knowingly collect personal information from children through the
  website.
</p>

<p>
  If you believe that a child has provided personal information to us,
  please contact us so that we can review the situation and take
  appropriate action.
</p>

<h2>9. Your choices</h2>

<p>
  Depending on the information and services involved, you may have
  rights or choices concerning your personal information, cookies,
  local storage, analytics and personalized advertising.
</p>

<p>
  You can also control or clear locally stored browser data through
  your browser settings.
</p>

<p>
  Where applicable, advertising and analytics providers may provide
  additional controls for managing their own data collection and
  personalization practices.
</p>

<h2>10. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>

<p>
  We may update this Privacy Policy when CreateLoom's features,
  services, analytics, advertising, affiliate relationships or legal
  requirements change.
</p>

<p>
  When we make changes, we will update the "Last updated" date shown
  at the beginning of this policy.
</p>

<h2>11. Contact</h2>

<p>
  If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how information
  is handled on CreateLoom, please contact us through the
  <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
</p>

<p class="notice">
  This Privacy Policy is intended to describe CreateLoom's current
  website practices. It is not legal advice. You should review the
  policy with a qualified legal professional if you begin collecting
  personal information, using analytics or advertising services,
  processing payments, operating affiliate programs, or introducing
  other data-processing features.
</p>
```

